.TH FERMI_SSO_PROBE 1 "2026-08-18" "requests-fermi-sso 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fermi_sso_probe \- verify a Fermilab single sign\-on login
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fermi_sso_probe
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ URL ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fermi_sso_probe
fetches
.I URL
through a
.BR FermiSSOSession (3)
and reports whether the Fermilab single sign\-on sequence actually completed.
.PP
This check is not redundant with the HTTP status code.
.B FermiSSOSession
returns the identity provider's login page with status 200 when credentials
are rejected, so a script that only inspects
.B resp.status_code
cannot tell a successful login from a failed one. The probe instead declares
success only when all of the following hold:
.RS
.IP \(bu 3
the final response URL is no longer on the identity provider host
.IP \(bu 3
the body no longer matches the choose\-authentication, login\-form, or
SAML postback patterns
.IP \(bu 3
the text given to
.B \-\-expect
is present, if that option was used
.RE
.PP
With no
.I URL
argument the probe fetches the Mu2e DocDB single sign\-on entry point,
.IR https://mu2e\-docdb.fnal.gov/cgi\-bin/sso/DocumentDatabase .
Note that
.I https://mu2e\-docdb.fnal.gov/
itself is an unprotected landing page and does not exercise the login flow.
Any other SSO\-protected URL may be given instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-u " NAME" "\fR, \fP" \-\-user " NAME"
Fermilab services account name.
.TP
.BI \-p " PASSWORD" "\fR, \fP" \-\-password " PASSWORD"
Password given directly on the command line. Convenient for interactive
one\-offs, but note that command lines are visible to every user on the
system through
.BR ps (1)
and are recorded in the shell history file. Prefer
.BR \-\-password\-env ,
an env file, or the interactive prompt for anything repeated or scripted.
.TP
.BI \-\-password\-env " NAME"
Read the password from the environment variable
.IR NAME .
It is an error if that variable is unset or empty.
.TP
.BI \-U " URL" "\fR, \fP" \-\-url " URL"
Equivalent to the positional
.I URL
argument.
.TP
.BI \-e " FILE" "\fR, \fP" \-\-env\-file " FILE"
Read settings from
.IR FILE .
It is an error if
.I FILE
does not exist. Without this option the probe looks for
.I ./.env
and then
.IR ~/.fermi_sso.env ,
using the first that exists.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-env\-file
Ignore env files entirely. Use this in cron and CI so a stray
.I .env
in the working directory cannot change the result.
.TP
.BI \-\-idp\-host " HOST"
Hostname of the identity provider, used to detect a login that stalled
without reaching the service provider. Defaults to
.IR pingprod.fnal.gov .
Set it to the empty string to disable that check when probing a site behind
a different IdP.
.TP
.BI \-x " TEXT" "\fR, \fP" \-\-expect " TEXT"
Require
.I TEXT
to appear in the final page body. Without this the probe only verifies that
the login sequence finished, not that the page is the one you wanted.
.TP
.BI \-o " FILE" "\fR, \fP" \-\-output " FILE"
Write the final response body to
.IR FILE ,
or to standard output if
.I FILE
is
.BR \- .
Diagnostics always go to standard error, so the body can be redirected
cleanly.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-prompt
Never prompt for a missing password; fail instead. Implied when standard
input is not a terminal.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the per\-request detail and print only the final verdict.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Enable wire\-level HTTP logging and
.B requests_fermi_sso
debug output. This prints request and response headers, including cookies.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH CREDENTIAL AND SETTING RESOLUTION
Every setting is resolved from the first source that supplies it, in this
order:
.RS
.IP 1. 3
command line options
.IP 2. 3
environment variables
.IP 3. 3
the env file
.IP 4. 3
built\-in defaults
.RE
.PP
The password has one extra step: if no source supplies it and standard input
is a terminal, the probe prompts for it without echo. An environment variable
set to the empty string counts as absent.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FERMI_USER
Services account name. Falls back to
.B USER
if unset.
.TP
.B FERMI_PASSWORD
Password. Read from the environment or from the env file.
.TP
.B FERMI_SSO_URL
Default URL to fetch.
.TP
.B FERMI_SSO_IDP_HOST
Default identity provider hostname.
.TP
.B FERMI_SSO_ENV_FILE
Path to the env file, overriding the default search.
.TP
.B FERMI_SSO_DEBUG
Set to
.B 1
to enable debug logging.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./.env
Env file searched first when
.B \-\-env\-file
is not given.
.TP
.I ~/.fermi_sso.env
Env file searched second.
.PP
Env file syntax is one
.BI KEY= value
per line. Blank lines and lines beginning with
.B #
are ignored, a leading
.B export
is stripped, and single\- or double\-quoted values have their quotes removed.
Quote any value containing
.BR # ,
or a trailing comment will be stripped from it. Because these files hold a
password, the probe warns when one is readable by group or other; keep them
at mode 600.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The login completed and all checks passed.
.TP
.B 1
The login did not complete, or the
.B \-\-expect
text was absent.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: no username, no password, a missing env file, or a password
containing a colon.
.SH EXAMPLES
Probe the default Mu2e DocDB entry point, prompting for the password:
.PP
.RS
.EX
fermi_sso_probe \-u myaccount
.EE
.RE
.PP
Probe a different SSO\-protected site and require known text on the page:
.PP
.RS
.EX
fermi_sso_probe \-u myaccount \-x "Welcome" https://example.fnal.gov/private
.EE
.RE
.PP
Non\-interactive check suitable for cron, with credentials in a mode\-600 file:
.PP
.RS
.EX
fermi_sso_probe \-\-env\-file ~/.fermi_sso.env \-n \-q
.EE
.RE
.PP
Save the fetched page while watching the full exchange:
.PP
.RS
.EX
fermi_sso_probe \-u myaccount \-d \-o /tmp/page.html 2> /tmp/trace.log
.EE
.RE
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.TP
.B still on the login form
The password was rejected, or the account requires multi\-factor
authentication. See LIMITATIONS.
.TP
.B still on the choose\-authentication page
The identity provider did not accept the password\-authentication selection.
The adapter identifier may have changed at the IdP.
.TP
.B stopped on the SAML postback form
Authentication succeeded but the assertion was not posted back to the
service provider.
.TP
.B stranded on pingprod.fnal.gov
The flow ended on the IdP at a page the library does not recognize, such as
an error or consent interstitial.
.TP
.B password contains ':'
.B FermiSSOSession
packs the credentials into a single
.RI \(dq user : pass \(dq
string and splits on every colon, so an embedded colon cannot be
represented. Use an account whose password has no colon.
.SH LIMITATIONS
The underlying library drives only the
.B ad..FormBased
adapter, which is the identity provider's
.RB \(dq "Services Username and Password" \(dq
option. Accounts enrolled in multi\-factor authentication cannot complete
this flow, because there is no path for a second factor. Non\-interactive
scripts generally need a service account provisioned for password
authentication.
.PP
Page recognition is done with regular expressions over the raw HTML. A markup
change at the identity provider will present as a login failure rather than
as a parse error.
.PP
.B FermiSSOSession
keeps its in\-flight state on the session object and is not safe to share
across threads. Use one session per thread.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1),
.BR ps (1)
.PP
Project documentation:
.I docs/HOWTO.md
in the source distribution.
.SH AUTHOR
Library by Marc Mengel <mengel@fnal.gov>. Probe utility added for the
Mu2e DocDB authentication work.
